    <section class="what-is-section">
        <div class="container">
            <div class="what-is-grid">
                <div class="what-is-content"> <span class="section-label">ELECTROMAGNETIC NDT FOR FERROMAGNETICS</span>
                    <h2>What is Near Field Testing (NFT) Tube Inspection?</h2>
                    <p class="lead">Near Field Testing (NFT) is a specialized low-frequency electromagnetic inspection technique optimized for ferromagnetic tubes (carbon steel, low alloy steel) commonly found in power plant boilers, economizers, HRSGs, and industrial process heaters where conventional eddy current testing faces challenges due to high magnetic permeability.</p>
                    <p>NFT operates at very low frequencies (50-500 Hz) compared to conventional eddy current testing (10 kHz - 6 MHz), generating electromagnetic fields that penetrate the full tube wall thickness in ferromagnetic materials. The probe consists of a small transmit coil energized with low-frequency AC and one or more receive coils positioned in the "near field" region (within approximately one coil diameter) where the electromagnetic field is predominantly reactive rather than radiative.</p>
                    <p>This near-field coupling creates unique advantages: (1) Deep penetration through ferromagnetic tube walls (3-15mm typical), (2) Equal sensitivity to inner diameter (ID) and outer diameter (OD) defects due to through-transmission detection, (3) Minimal interference from magnetic permeability variations that plague conventional ECT, and (4) Reduced support plate signals enabling clearer defect identification. NFT detects wall loss from corrosion/erosion (general and localized), pitting (ID and OD surfaces), denting, and some crack indications depending on orientation and frequency selection.</p>
                    <div class="feature-list">
                        <div class="feature-item"> <i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i>
                            <div> <strong>Low-Frequency Penetration</strong>
                                <p>50-500 Hz operation penetrates ferromagnetic tube walls providing full thickness inspection</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="feature-item"> <i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i>
                            <div> <strong>Through-Transmission Detection</strong>
                                <p>Separate transmit/receive coils measure signal attenuation from wall loss and defects</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="feature-item"> <i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i>
                            <div> <strong>Permeability Insensitivity</strong>
                                <p>Low frequencies minimize magnetic permeability interference common in ferromagnetic ECT</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="feature-item"> <i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i>
