                                        <p>Economizer tubes operating in 100-200°C feedwater temperature range with single-phase high-velocity flow (2-5 m/s) are highly vulnerable to FAC—dissolution of protective magnetite layer causing rapid wall loss (0.1-1.0 mm/year). EPRI estimates FAC causes 10-20% of fossil plant forced outages. NFT enables proactive FAC monitoring identifying high-wastage zones for chemistry optimization (pH, oxygen, hydrazine control), orifice installation to reduce velocity, or metallurgy upgrade to FAC-resistant materials (chrome-moly alloys). Predictive NFT trending prevents catastrophic economizer failures requiring 4-8 week outage and $1M-5M repair.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="standards"> <strong>Applicable Standards:</strong> <span class="standard-tag">ASME Sec I</span> <span class="standard-tag">EPRI FAC Guidelines</span> <span class="standard-tag">NACE SP0590</span> <span class="standard-tag">ASME PCC-2 Art 5.1</span> </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div> <!-- HRSG Systems Tab -->
