                                </ul>
                                <div class="app-highlight"> <i class="fas fa-sync-alt"></i>
                                    <div> <strong>Cyclic Operation Damage:</strong>
                                        <p>HRSG units providing peak power or load-following service experience daily or multiple-daily start-stop cycles (vs. baseload 24/7 operation). Rapid heating/cooling cycles induce thermal stresses causing low-cycle fatigue cracking at tube-to-header welds, rolled joints, and constraint points. Cyclic units accumulate 300-1000 start equivalents per year versus 10-50 for baseload—accelerating fatigue life consumption. NFT combined with tube sample metallographic analysis (removed tube destructive testing) validates remaining fatigue life and supports fitness-for-service evaluation per API 579-1 Part 10 (Remaining Life Assessment). Enables transition from time-based tube replacement (every 100K-200K operating hours) to condition-based strategies optimizing capital expenditures.</p>
                                    </div>
                                </div>
                                <div class="standards"> <strong>Applicable Standards:</strong> <span class="standard-tag">ASME Sec I</span> <span class="standard-tag">HRSG User Group</span> <span class="standard-tag">EPRI HRSG Guidelines</span> <span class="standard-tag">ISO 12952-3</span> </div>
                            </div>
