                                <h3>Industrial Process Heater & Fired Heater Tubes</h3>
                                <p>Refinery crude unit, coker, and hydrocracker fired heaters with carbon steel convection section tubes experience internal coking, external fireside corrosion, and high-temperature creep. Chemical plant steam reformers, ethylene crackers, and ammonia primary reformers operate at extreme temperatures (800-1100°C) requiring alloy tubes but with carbon steel preheater/convection sections. NFT detects tube degradation preventing failures that cause unit shutdown, process contamination, and safety incidents.</p>
